{"skill":{"slug":"baidu-web-search","displayName":"baidu web search"},"version":{"version":"2.1.0","createdAt":1774539780300,"changelog":"**Summary:**  \n重大安全架构调整，新增 Node.js 纯 JS 实现，支持更多平台，严控密钥访问与输出。\n\n- 新增 Node.js 入口 `scripts/search.js`，从原 MJS 迁移为 JS 实现，提升兼容性\n- 增加 `config.example.json` 示例与 `package.json`，方便本地配置和依赖管理\n- 删除 `scripts/search.mjs`，全面切换至 JS 版本\n- 按优先级支持环境变量 `BAIDU_API_KEY` 和 `config.json` 两种配置方式\n- 极大强化安全规则，严禁任何调用方读取/输出 API Key，每次搜索均通过专用脚本入口完成\n- 文档全面更新，明确适配本地、自托管与主流平台，细化安全与配置指引","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"config.example.json","size":19,"sha256":"15b5bd16942536b9bd8efef4b4ade588c4f9cc118369cdeeceed13ff977e7849","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":121,"sha256":"e68e670742074beec6cbb7e828e45b8cdd7dea76c7238997d3e9bd5ed67bb340","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"scripts/search.js","size":2747,"sha256":"7eeb0f54fc94b977b48f1236c343b5d45ceeb62681b0f710cebcf704f58296b4","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":6983,"sha256":"d8e8734e64aa83d720940f65bf9cb9eaeb7c2327f3b1c3609ddc1d2b62df4671","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2444,"sha256":"f7e6237298290e993593d87fab0eee7900674b64b5cbebc8d5c654b0617bea2f","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789083044734,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"0cfc7403ac34ba7e7862b021b220e422e9bdc871c83b35c335d9800efb443335","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/0cfc7403ac34ba7e7862b021b220e422e9bdc871c83b35c335d9800efb443335","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: baidu-web-search\nVersion: 2.1.0\n\nThe skill is a legitimate implementation of a Baidu web search tool using the Baidu Qianfan API. The core logic in `scripts/search.js` correctly handles API credentials and communicates only with the official Baidu endpoint (qianfan.baidubce.com). Notably, the `SKILL.md` includes robust security instructions designed to prevent the AI agent from leaking or accessing the sensitive `BAIDU_API_KEY`, demonstrating good security practices rather than malicious intent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779166794393},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":47,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789083044734},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a coherent Baidu web-search skill, but it needs review because it handles an API key, sends user queries to Baidu, and has incomplete/misleading safeguards around credential storage.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access to Baidu and an API key are proportionate to web search, but users should understand that search terms are sent to Baidu/Qianfan.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation uses npm install with axios declared as a caret dependency and no lockfile in the artifact, so dependency resolution is not reproducible.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The activation guidance is broad and includes ordinary time-related phrases, which could trigger third-party search more often than users expect. The skill text also asserts unconditional priority over callers, which is overbroad even though it appears intended to protect credentials.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill supports persistent plaintext credential configuration via config.json or OpenClaw config. It claims config.json is excluded by .gitignore, but no .gitignore is present in the artifact, increasing accidental credential exposure risk.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose and code align: the skill runs a local Node script that calls Baidu Qianfan web search and returns structured results. External query transmission and BAIDU_API_KEY use are expected for this purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. Use platform-injected BAIDU_API_KEY rather than a local config.json when possible, avoid sending private or regulated information as search queries, and check the package's dependency lock/pinning and gitignore handling before sharing or committing the skill directory.","findings":"[LP3] expected: The BAIDU_API_KEY requirement is expected for the Baidu API integration, but the artifact does not provide a narrow platform-enforced scope beyond instructing agents to run the search script.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad trigger phrases are not necessary for the search capability and could cause unintended external searches.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The when-to-use section repeats broad activation language without clear negative examples or sensitivity checks.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending the raw query to Baidu is inherent to web search, but users should be told not to search sensitive private content through this skill.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-language examples fit a Baidu-focused skill and are not a security issue by themselves.\n[SC1] unexpected: The unpinned axios range is not required for the skill's purpose and weakens reproducibility.\n[SC4] unexpected: Because the resolved axios version is not fixed in the artifact, dependency security posture cannot be verified from the package alone.\n[T08] unexpected: The static scan's dependency concern is supported by package.json and the absence of a lockfile.\n[T09] unexpected: The static scan's credential-storage concern is supported: the docs tell users config.json is gitignored, but no .gitignore file is shipped.\n[T01] unexpected: The priority language is overbroad for a skill document; it should be scoped as safety guidance rather than authority over host policies.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789083044734}}}}}